{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/99230-lucifuge-s-reconciliation","id":99230,"title":"Lucifuge's Reconciliation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-26T09:31:53-07:00","id":99230,"title":"Lucifuge's Reconciliation","content":"So I was doing a bit of Dream Catchers and I noticed something about the Reconciliation.<br /> <br /> The Hunter the Vigil core doesn't actually mention if they're any more/less aggressive towards monsters than the other factions. That only becomes explicit in later books.<br /> <br /> Now I know that the section on The Reconciliation in all other books were by a different author, so what I'm wondering is if it was always the authorial intent that the Reconciliation were the standard kill-all-monsters fanatics faction. Or where they supposed to have similar views as The Denial towards monsters and only have different views towards their own heritage?<br /> <br /> Can anyone think of anything that might support either possibility?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T19:30:24-07:00","id":133056,"title":"","content":"Perosnally I don't even think that they are about &quot;Kill all monsters.&quot; I think that they just have less of a grey area. <br /> <br /> The Denial sees an &quot;evil monster&quot; they might a) try to kill it or b) try to convince it to change its ways. They'll generally choose B<br /> and there's about a billion ways they could go about that. Basically they'll try harder to avoid the 'kill it' option cause they themselves know that deep down they're monsters too.<br /> <br /> The Denial sees a monster that isn't causing harm. Leave it alone, watch it.<br /> <br /> The Reconciliation sees an &quot;evil monster&quot;, thing's gotta go. Period. It doin' it's evil deeds is standing in the way of the Lucifuge clearing Lucifer's slate. <br /> <br /> The Reconciliation sees a monster that isn't causing harm. Leave it alone, watch it. The _second_ it does something evil, it goes.<br /> If it's performing no evil acts it's not smearin' Lucifer's name. <br /> <br /> At least that's how I interperet it. I could be wrong and probably am but that's how I like to see it. I kinda like that the Lucifuge doens't just kill everything and dont' think that the Reconciliation should be all about killing everything either, just they're more open to the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2988-krivonyak","name":"Krivonyak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}